    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρί-δουλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thrice a slave,</i> Ach. Tat.<i><span class="en">
				8.1
			</span></i>; by descent, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἐὰν τρίτης . . μητρὸς φανῶ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1063
				</span></i>
			; as slave of a slave's slave, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				244
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῦγος τ.</span> a leash <i>of slaves,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				576
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπάρθενος.</span></div>
